### File Handling in Java: FileReader and BufferedReader

- **`FileReader`:** Character stream class for reading text files character-by-character.
- **`BufferedReader`:** Wraps around a `Reader` to buffer characters, providing efficient reading of characters, arrays, and whole lines via `readLine()`.

```java
try (BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new FileReader("input.txt"))) {
    String line;
    while ((line = br.readLine()) != null) {
        System.out.println(line);
    }
}
```

$$\therefore \text{Buffering significantly reduces physical disk I/O operations, multiplying read throughput.}$$
